# Cloudflare response headers.
# Content-Security-Policy (01/11/2026): ENFORCED on the pages of the main app (/, the v2 redirect,
# privacy). Scripts only from our origin, the Firebase SDK (gstatic), Google sign-in (apis.google.com)
# and Cloudflare Web Analytics; inline scripts only by sha256 (the two in index.html, the v2 redirect,
# the road book's print script in v2/lib/rideout.mjs); no inline onclick (js/lrcact.js). Images,
# fetches and styles stay open to https (map tiles, weather, routing come from many hosts).
# test/csp.test.mjs keeps the hashes and hosts in sync with the pages: change both together.
# The classic app (/classica/) keeps the old REPORT-ONLY policy until it is switched off.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), geolocation=(self)

